    {
      "body": "You are right, that is a fourth site and it cannot honour `val` either. Two things to add before it moves.\n\n**The \"no other reader\" argument needs the other branch too.** `get_grad_norm_direct` reaches that masking from two places, and only one of them produces a fresh tensor:\n\n```python\n# norm_type == inf\ntotal_norm = total_norm_cuda[0]            # a view into total_norm_cuda\n# else\ntotal_norm = total_norm_cuda**(1. / norm_type)   # fresh\n```\n\nSo `masked_fill_` on the inf path also writes into `total_norm_cuda`. It is still safe, because nothing reads `total_norm_cuda` after that line and the function returns immediately, but the justification should say so rather than resting on the finite-norm path alone.\n\n**Dtypes agree on both paths.** The inf branch comes off `FloatTensor`, so fp32; the finite branch off `get_norm_dtype()`, fp32 or fp64. `masked_fill_` keeps the input dtype and `torch.where` promotes to the same thing, which matches what you measured.\n\nTaking your suggestion: this PR stays the one-line `val` fix. Happy to fold the stage3 site in here instead if you would rather have one PR, just say which you prefer.",
      "created_at": "2026-09-03T21:35:12Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/deepspeedai/DeepSpeed/pull/8386#issuecomment-5532447423",
      "id": 5532447423,
      "updated_at": "2026-09-03T21:35:12Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "vineethsaivs"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "Separate, I'd say. This one is a one line change with a self-contained argument. The stage3 swap turns an allocating `torch.where` into an in place write on `total_norm_cuda[0]`, which is the aliasing you just described, so it wants its own diff rather than riding along under this title.\n\nYou are right that my justification only covered the else branch. `total_norm = total_norm_cuda[0]` is a view, so on the inf path the write lands in `total_norm_cuda`; nothing reads it afterwards and the function returns on the next line, but that is the argument there, not the fresh-tensor one.\n",
      "created_at": "2026-09-04T00:30:38Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/deepspeedai/DeepSpeed/pull/8386#issuecomment-5533933443",
      "id": 5533933443,
      "updated_at": "2026-09-04T00:30:38Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "ebarkhordar"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "Agreed on both counts. Keeping this one at the single line, and I will open the stage3 `torch.where` change separately so the aliasing argument gets its own diff rather than hiding under this title.",
      "created_at": "2026-09-08T16:58:36Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/deepspeedai/DeepSpeed/pull/8386#issuecomment-5588826644",
      "id": 5588826644,
